{
 "method": "Photon MC (2.2M source photons) in 30 cm water cube, 10x10 cm2 SSD-100 Co-60-like beam; fluences scored as track length/volume in the r=1 cm, 0.2 cm cylinder at 5 cm, normalized to Phi0=1/(4pi*105^2). Compton sampled with Klein-Nishina, Rayleigh treated as forward-elastic, photoelectric/pair absorbed. L2/L3 obtained by weighting the scored photon fluence spectra with interaction cross sections (primary lines at 1.1732/1.3325 MeV) and KN electron kinematics. Electron layer from CSDA slowing-down spectra with M\u00f8ller knock-ons (delta rays). Dose = collision kerma (CPE, beta=1); kerma from mass energy-transfer/absorption coefficients; PDD from depth-dose Kcol curve (dmax~0.5 cm); s_w,air taken as standard 60Co Spencer-Attix value.",
 "data_sources": "NIST-XCOM-like total, coherent and energy-absorption mass attenuation coefficients for water; Klein-Nishina formula for Compton; power-law fits for photoelectric and pair. Stopping powers: ICRU-37/ESTAR-like collision stopping powers for water and air; Spencer-Attix s_w,air for 60Co = 1.133 (IAEA TRS-398). G-values from water mu_en/mu_tr data (~0.003 at 1.25 MeV).",
